      "Representation and Contracts"
    ]
  ],
  """\
Examples from the technology estate; a site build selects its \
technologies. Availability varies by capability.\
"""
]

[[section]]
title = "Identity and security"
headline = "Explicit trust at each boundary"
screen = """\
Parties and accepted identities\nIndependent inbound and outbound \
identity\nMutual TLS and encrypted embedded storage\
"""
voice = "male"
power = false
narration = """\
Trust is explicit at Xmip’s boundaries. Parties carry identities, receive \
locations define what they accept, and outbound exchanges use their own \
identity. Certificate authentication, protected storage connections and \
encrypted embedded data give that architecture concrete foundations.\
"""
sources = [
  "doc/decision/ADR-0019-identity-parties-and-direction.md",
  "doc/architecture/estate-map.md",
  "doc/decision/ADR-0063-xmip-encrypts-its-traffic-and-its-storage.md"
]
note = ""
layout = [
  "split",
  "Trust at the boundary",
  [
    [
      "Inbound",
      "Declare what is accepted",
      """\
Receive Locations name accepted mechanisms and Parties. A Party holds \
identities for its exchanges.\
"""
    ],
    [
      "Outbound",
      "Present the chosen identity",
      "The security model gives Send Locations their own outward identity."
    ]
  ],
  """\
Working foundations include certificate authentication, mutual TLS for \
Storage and encrypted embedded storage.\
"""
]

[[section]]
title = "Xmip Storage and the Ledger"
headline = "Work belongs to the platform"
screen = """\
A shared persistence boundary\nEmbedded or remotely reached \
Storage\nMessages, Journeys and pending work\
"""
voice = "female"
power = false
narration = """\
Xmip Storage gives work a persistent home. A small deployment can host \
storage within its own node, while other nodes reach it over mutual TLS. \
The ledger holds messages, journeys and pending work, separate from \
administration and audit concerns.\
"""
sources = [
  "doc/architecture/deployment-model.md",
  "doc/architecture/estate-map.md"
]
note = ""
layout = [
  "three",
  "Storage with clear responsibilities",
  [
    [
      "Runtime",
      "The Ledger",
      "Messages, Journeys and pending work."
    ],
    [
      "Administration",
      "The operating setup",
      "Configuration and administrative state."
    ],
    [
      "Audit",
      "The recorded history",
      "Actions and outcomes form a distinct data domain."
    ]
  ],
  """\
Xmip Storage is the persistence boundary. Use an embedded Storage node or \
reach Storage over mutual TLS.\
"""
]

[[section]]
title = "Deployment and node roles"
headline = "Compose the runtime for the site"
screen = """\
Select target, roles and technologies\nCombine stages in an Executing \
node\nPlace storage and observation deliberately\
"""
voice = "male"
power = false
narration = """\
A deployment is a composition of roles and capabilities. Executing brings \
the message stages together in one process, while other roles serve \
storage, observation and operation. Site builds select the target and \
technologies; configuration determines what the node starts.\
"""
sources = [
